// Black walnut, number 4. Its structure is measured from Mokume's black walnut
// (Juglans nigra); its color is Mokume's moved in Oklab by L +0.045, chroma
// x1.7 and hue +6 degrees, so a flat-sawn face averages L 0.535, chroma 0.048,
// hue 57. Mokume's photographs gave a gray L 0.49, chroma 0.028: sanded
// European walnut measures L* 56.8, a* 6.6, b* 13.0 (Liu and Timar 2022;
// Oklab L 0.63, chroma 0.040, hue 58), black walnut being the darker, and Poly
// Haven's walnut veneers (CC0, calibrated albedo) L 0.55, chroma 0.056, hue 58
// and, a paler, steamed-looking lot, L 0.68, chroma 0.042, hue 65. The sapwood
