// A wood's stand-in: its earlywood and latewood mixed in Oklab at its
// latewood fraction, the rings averaged out, and greyed as weatheredColor
// greys it; the pores, knots and sapwood are left out.
woodStandIn(earlyColor, lateColor, latewoodFraction, weather) {
  ringsLab = color.rgb2oklab(color.mixOklab(earlyColor, lateColor, latewoodFraction));
  return color.oklab2rgb(ringsLab + (color.rgb2oklab([0.60, 0.58, 0.54]) - ringsLab) * (0.375 * max(weather, 0)));
}

// Wood of linear colour c charred `char` mm deep: browned, by [0.52, 0.38,
// 0.28] for every 0.3 mm, and blackening toward charcoal, linear [0.02, 0.018,
// 0.016], 1 - exp(-(char / 0.6)^2) of the way, so a light torching browns and
// a millimetre of char is black. Judged.
charredColor(c, char) {
  browned = c * [pow(0.52, char / 0.3), pow(0.38, char / 0.3), pow(0.28, char / 0.3)];
  return browned + ([0.02, 0.018, 0.016] - browned) * (1 - exp(-(char / 0.6) * (char / 0.6)));
