/// zebrawood(axisOrigin, axisDir, look): Zebrawood: light gold with narrow dark
/// brown stripes, the rings' latewood, sharp and uneven. The two colours are
/// The Wood Database's light and dark stripes; the structure is judged.
zebrawood(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir, look) {
  return species(zebrawoodNumber, axisOrigin, axisDir, look);
}
zebrawood(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir) {
  return zebrawood(axisOrigin, axisDir, defaultLook);
}

/// lacewood(axisOrigin, axisDir, look): Brazilian lacewood: reddish brown with
/// very wide pale rays that make the lace on quarter-sawn faces. The colour is
/// The Wood Database's; the rays are judged.
lacewood(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir, look) {
  return species(lacewoodNumber, axisOrigin, axisDir, look);
}
lacewood(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir) {
  return lacewood(axisOrigin, axisDir, defaultLook);
}

/// spruce(axisOrigin, axisDir, look): Sitka spruce: a pale cream softwood,
/// tight 1.2 mm rings darkening gradually into a narrow latewood, sparse resin
/// canals, sapwood that shades into the heartwood, and small knots; light
/// yellows it.
spruce(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir, look) {
  return species(spruceNumber, axisOrigin, axisDir, look);
}
spruce(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir) {
  return spruce(axisOrigin, axisDir, defaultLook);
}

/// westernRedCedar(axisOrigin, axisDir, look): Western red cedar: a soft,
/// light brown to reddish-brown softwood with abrupt dark latewood lines,
/// darker streaks, nearly white narrow sapwood, no resin canals, and knots; it
/// darkens in light.
westernRedCedar(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir, look) {
  return species(westernRedCedarNumber, axisOrigin, axisDir, look);
}
westernRedCedar(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir) {
  return westernRedCedar(axisOrigin, axisDir, defaultLook);
}

/// aromaticCedar(axisOrigin, axisDir, look): Aromatic cedar: purple-red
/// heartwood with pale yellow sapwood in streaks, fine even texture, gradual
/// rings, no resin canals and many small knots; light fades it to a reddish
/// brown within weeks.
aromaticCedar(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir, look) {
  return species(aromaticCedarNumber, axisOrigin, axisDir, look);
}
aromaticCedar(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir) {
  return aromaticCedar(axisOrigin, axisDir, defaultLook);
}

/// holly(axisOrigin, axisDir, look): American holly: the whitest wood, ivory
/// white and diffuse-porous with rings barely there, fine pores and rays that
/// range from fine to wide; light yellows it slightly.
holly(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir, look) {
  return species(hollyNumber, axisOrigin, axisDir, look);
}
holly(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir) {
  return holly(axisOrigin, axisDir, defaultLook);
}

/// weatheredOak(axisOrigin, axisDir): oak left out in the weather for years:
/// silver grey over the grain, the softer earlywood worn back so the latewood
/// stands proud by about 0.4 mm, and drying checks opening along the grain.
/// The relief is render-only displacement. Returns material, color.
weatheredOak(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir) {
  return whiteOak(axisOrigin, axisDir, [0.3, 0, 1]);
}

/// weatheredWalnut(axisOrigin, axisDir): weathered walnut, the soft latewood
/// standing only about 0.25 mm proud. Returns material, color.
weatheredWalnut(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir) {
  return walnut(axisOrigin, axisDir, [0.3, 0, 1]);
}

/// weatheredPine(axisOrigin, axisDir, knotScale): weathered pine, the hard
/// latewood bands standing about 0.8 mm proud as they do on an old deck or
/// fence board, with the knots of pine(). Returns material, color.
weatheredPine(@point axisOrigin, @direction(axisOrigin) axisDir, knotScale) {
  return pine(axisOrigin, axisDir, knotScale, [0.3, 0, 1]);
}

// ===========================================================================
// ===========================================================================
// Ready-made
// ===========================================================================

// One zero-argument overload per species, at its default look with the stem
// through the origin along +Z, so the material browser can show it; the
// annotation marks the name, so the datum forms above are the same entry.
// Adjust opens the stem's origin and direction into gizmos; see
// doc/material_composition.md, "Design: parameters on materials".

/// White oak, stem along +Z through the origin, at its default look. Returns
/// material and colour.
@material whiteOak() {
  m, c = whiteOak([0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 1]);
  return m, c;
}

